Creep!

33
00:03:14,710 --> 00:03:16,480
Are you all right?

34
00:03:18,550 --> 00:03:22,890
-Pervert!
-I'm okay, but my camera's dead.

35
00:03:22,890 --> 00:03:25,890
I wanted some bittersweet memories
of the days of my youth,

36
00:03:25,890 --> 00:03:27,730
so I had to take a bit of a risk...

37
00:03:27,730 --> 00:03:30,220
-Hey Tanabe!
-Huh?

38
00:03:31,230 --> 00:03:32,900
That rumor about Momo-chan...

39
00:03:32,900 --> 00:03:35,400
that she used to work part-time
in a cabaret club in college...

40
00:03:35,400 --> 00:03:37,170
Is it for real?!

41
00:03:37,170 --> 00:03:40,670
It bothers me so much
I can't study at all!

42
00:03:40,670 --> 00:03:43,340
Calm down guys.

43
00:03:43,340 --> 00:03:46,340
Give me a little more time to check it out.

44
00:03:46,340 --> 00:03:49,750
I'll find proof before graduation.

45
00:03:52,680 --> 00:03:55,020
I swear it on my grandpa's good name.

46
00:03:57,360 --> 00:04:00,690
Who's your grandpa?

47
00:04:00,690 --> 00:04:03,690
He's a railway employee.

48
00:04:03,690 --> 00:04:05,930
-Hmm...
-Hmm...
-Hmm...

49
00:04:05,930 --> 00:04:07,530
Let's go.

50
00:04:07,530 --> 00:04:08,520
-Yeah.
-Yeah.
-Yeah.

51
00:04:10,870 --> 00:04:12,460
A cabaret club, huh?

52
00:04:15,370 --> 00:04:18,840
And the one who got the idea for this

53
00:04:18,840 --> 00:04:22,710
was Franz Schubert of Austria.

54
00:04:22,710 --> 00:04:24,650
-And so...
-Huh?

55
00:04:25,880 --> 00:04:27,510
Tanaka-kun!

56
00:04:28,720 --> 00:04:31,220
Are you paying attention?

57
00:04:31,220 --> 00:04:32,220
Umm...

58
00:04:32,220 --> 00:04:34,390
Maybe you've been studying too hard.

59
00:04:34,390 --> 00:04:36,490
You have to relax sometimes.

60
00:04:38,160 --> 00:04:39,750
Yes.

61
00:04:56,350 --> 00:04:59,710
-Which school do you wanna go to?
-Huh? Oh...

62
00:05:03,020 --> 00:05:06,510
I'm trying for Tachi High.

63
00:05:09,030 --> 00:05:11,360
I'm trying for Tokutake High.

64
00:05:11,360 --> 00:05:12,400
Hey Tanaka...

65
00:05:12,400 --> 00:05:14,200
-Hit me.
-Huh?

66
00:05:14,200 --> 00:05:18,400
Haven't you wanted to hit me?

67
00:05:20,200 --> 00:05:23,880
Err...Not anymore.

68
00:05:23,880 --> 00:05:24,860
And before?

69
00:05:33,050 --> 00:05:35,220
You can't hit me?

70
00:05:35,220 --> 00:05:36,650
Coward!

71
00:05:39,990 --> 00:05:41,830
What was that?

72
00:05:41,830 --> 00:05:45,060
Your punch is like a girl's.

73
00:06:05,680 --> 00:06:08,020
People who create things

74
00:06:08,020 --> 00:06:11,680
must express their feelings clearly
or it's not good...

75
00:06:13,190 --> 00:06:15,090
My old man used to say that.

76
00:06:17,030 --> 00:06:18,090
So long.

77
00:06:22,700 --> 00:06:23,760
Hyodo-kun!

78
00:06:27,370 --> 00:06:28,800
See you around.

79
00:06:30,710 --> 00:06:31,800
Yeah.

80
00:06:42,150 --> 00:06:46,520
As expected, Momoko-sensei broke
into tears during graduation ceremonies.

81
00:07:05,180 --> 00:07:09,510
And high school entrance exams
ended without much fanfare.

82
00:07:11,180 --> 00:07:13,180
Yukio!

83
00:07:13,180 --> 00:07:16,180
Hurry or you'll be late
for the entrance ceremony!

84
00:07:17,360 --> 00:07:19,190
I know!

85
00:07:29,870 --> 00:07:30,200
"Private Ichieda Academy
Senior High School"

86
00:07:30,200 --> 00:07:35,040
"Private Ichieda Academy
Senior High School"

87
00:07:30,200 --> 00:07:35,040
From today, you are students
of Ichieda Academy

88
00:07:35,040 --> 00:07:39,140
here to study,
participate in sports and clubs.

89
00:07:39,140 --> 00:07:44,810
Osamu Kido, whose mentor,
Karl Goch, treated like a son...

90
00:07:51,820 --> 00:07:51,990
"Anime Research Society"

91
00:07:51,990 --> 00:07:56,260
"Anime Research Society"

92
00:07:51,990 --> 00:07:56,260
Hey, you seem like one of our kind.

93
00:07:56,260 --> 00:07:58,800
"Anime Research Society"

94
00:07:56,260 --> 00:07:58,800
No thanks. I don't intend to join a club.

95
00:07:58,800 --> 00:07:59,000
No thanks. I don't intend to join a club.

96
00:07:59,000 --> 00:08:01,170
Hey Koyuki!

97
00:08:01,170 --> 00:08:03,330
Hey Saku!

98
00:08:03,330 --> 00:08:05,840
Look at your hair!

99
00:08:05,840 --> 00:08:08,340
Well, I'm in high school now,
so I changed it.

100
00:08:08,340 --> 00:08:10,680
Don't go trying to look sexy.

101
00:08:10,680 --> 00:08:11,370
Huh?

102
00:08:13,180 --> 00:08:15,010
Lemme at you!

103
00:08:15,010 --> 00:08:16,850
-Hah!
-Hey!

104
00:08:16,850 --> 00:08:19,720
Shaddup! Trying to act grown-up!

105
00:08:19,720 --> 00:08:21,690
It's 100 years too early, kid!

106
00:08:21,690 --> 00:08:24,660
Hey, that's mean, Chiba-kun! Stop it!

107
00:08:30,030 --> 00:08:34,100
Geez! It took me an hour this morning.

108
00:08:34,100 --> 00:08:35,860
Huh? One hour?

109
00:08:38,640 --> 00:08:42,970
Senpai! I'm just not good
at signing up members!

110
00:08:42,970 --> 00:08:47,140
Shut up! If our activities end up
in the red, it'll be your fault!

111
00:08:47,140 --> 00:08:50,310
Moreover...the sign-up fee is too high.

112
00:08:50,310 --> 00:08:53,150
-Umm...
-Huh?
-Huh?

113
00:08:55,650 --> 00:08:57,320
Umm...Kikata-kun...

114
00:08:57,320 --> 00:08:59,720
You should give up already.

115
00:09:01,160 --> 00:09:04,300
Yusuke, he's the one...

116
00:09:04,300 --> 00:09:06,200
Yeah, I know.

117
00:09:12,170 --> 00:09:14,000
He just up and left...

118
00:09:14,000 --> 00:09:17,010
-I guess we'll be going, too...
-Hey!

119
00:09:17,010 --> 00:09:19,510
You're Yukio Tanaka,
the sophomore in Group 4?

120
00:09:19,510 --> 00:09:23,010
You'll pass out tickets in his place.

121
00:09:23,010 --> 00:09:25,350
Why me?

122
00:09:34,190 --> 00:09:36,890
Uh! Yeah!

123
00:09:40,800 --> 00:09:42,800
You open up the door with negative aura

124
00:09:42,800 --> 00:09:45,000
-Saku and I finished our entrance exams

125
00:09:42,800 --> 00:09:45,000
-You open up the door with negative aura

126
00:09:45,000 --> 00:09:46,140
-and we'll be concentrating
100% on the band.

127
00:09:45,000 --> 00:09:46,140
-You say future is murky indeed...

128
00:09:46,140 --> 00:09:49,110
-and we'll be concentrating
100% on the band.

129
00:09:46,140 --> 00:09:49,110
-I'm sick of hearing gripe.

130
00:09:49,110 --> 00:09:50,980
Open up the door with negative aura

131
00:09:50,980 --> 00:09:51,310
-I can't keep practicing
on Saito-san's guitar forever...

132
00:09:50,980 --> 00:09:51,310
-Open up the door with negative aura

133
00:09:51,310 --> 00:09:52,310
-I can't keep practicing
on Saito-san's guitar forever...

134
00:09:51,310 --> 00:09:52,310
-If you never change

135
00:09:52,310 --> 00:09:55,150
-I can't keep practicing
on Saito-san's guitar forever...

136
00:09:52,310 --> 00:09:55,150
-I think there is no way my life fizzle out...

137
00:09:55,150 --> 00:09:58,320
-And I've been wanting my own guitar.

138
00:09:55,150 --> 00:09:58,320
-I think there is no way my life fizzle out...

139
00:09:58,320 --> 00:10:01,320
Oh yeah? Then I'll go
with you to shop around.

140
00:10:01,320 --> 00:10:03,150
There's one I wanna see, too.

141
00:10:03,150 --> 00:10:04,490
Really?

142
00:10:04,490 --> 00:10:06,660
I'll catch up with you later.

143
00:10:06,660 --> 00:10:07,990
What about you guys?

144
00:10:07,990 --> 00:10:09,830
This is all I need.

145
00:10:09,830 --> 00:10:11,160
You being sarcastic?

146
00:10:21,170 --> 00:10:24,510
Say, don't you get nervous
going into a music store?

147
00:10:24,510 --> 00:10:25,810
You'll get used to it.

148
00:10:28,510 --> 00:10:30,710
So, what are you after?

149
00:10:34,190 --> 00:10:37,120
A Stratocaster...Jaguar...

150
00:10:37,120 --> 00:10:39,460
Jazz Master...

151
00:10:39,460 --> 00:10:41,890
Explorer...SG...

152
00:10:43,290 --> 00:10:45,460
Makes me want all of them!

153
00:10:45,460 --> 00:10:50,970
-This one...a Kayama Yuzo
by Mosrite is good.
-Oh?

154
00:10:50,970 --> 00:10:55,340
No need to rush into it.
We can check out other places.

155
00:10:55,340 --> 00:10:56,600
You're right.

156
00:10:58,310 --> 00:10:59,780
He dissed me!

157
00:11:06,820 --> 00:11:08,150
Umm...

158
00:11:08,150 --> 00:11:11,160
My friends and I are gonna start a band...

159
00:11:11,160 --> 00:11:15,330
We need something called an effector.

160
00:11:15,330 --> 00:11:21,000
Umm...My friend said something like
what Pink Floyd uses might work for us...

161
00:11:21,000 --> 00:11:25,340
Do you even know what an effector is?

162
00:11:25,340 --> 00:11:28,510
Not only that...get real.

163
00:11:28,510 --> 00:11:32,180
You can't produce a sound like
Pink Floyd on a 5000-yen budget.

164
00:11:32,180 --> 00:11:37,680
Oh, it doesn't really
have to be Pink Floyd...

165
00:11:37,680 --> 00:11:39,240
Make up your mind!

166
00:11:49,690 --> 00:11:54,830
Did you see last night's Time Machine?
Van Halen was on.

167
00:11:54,830 --> 00:11:56,200
Yes.

168
00:11:56,200 --> 00:12:02,870
-Ryusuke-kun...That clerk is scary.
-There's no one like them these days...

169
00:12:02,870 --> 00:12:05,380
A lot of 'em are like that.

170
00:12:05,380 --> 00:12:07,040
Excuse me...

171
00:12:07,040 --> 00:12:11,380
I want to try out this
pretty Tiger-eye Les Paul.

172
00:12:11,380 --> 00:12:15,890
Ryusuke-kun...this one says 'ask' on
the tag. How much do you think it is?

173
00:12:15,890 --> 00:12:17,720
1,080,000 yen.

174
00:12:17,720 --> 00:12:18,720
Huh?

175
00:12:18,720 --> 00:12:24,830
That's vintage 1959 Les Paul
made by the legendary Tom Murphy.

176
00:12:24,830 --> 00:12:25,730
Yeah...

177
00:12:25,730 --> 00:12:26,730
Hmm...

178
00:12:26,730 --> 00:12:28,250
Hey, keep your hands off!

179
00:12:31,070 --> 00:12:33,970
I was going to use this as a down payment.

180
00:12:35,740 --> 00:12:37,510
Just a minute...

181
00:12:37,510 --> 00:12:40,510
Ryusuke-kun! How'd you
get so much money?

182
00:12:40,510 --> 00:12:44,570
I was gonna go to the fish farm
after this to buy fish.

183
00:12:59,860 --> 00:13:02,730
Takano-san...Y-You're amazing.

184
00:13:11,540 --> 00:13:14,010
Okay, this guitar is prepped.

185
00:13:17,720 --> 00:13:19,550
Koyuki, play.

186
00:13:19,550 --> 00:13:21,520
Huh? Ryusuke-kun, you play.

187
00:13:23,890 --> 00:13:25,150
Yeah?

188
00:13:26,720 --> 00:13:30,220
Can't get a true sound
if it's wired like this.

189
00:13:56,020 --> 00:13:58,360
H-How is it?

190
00:13:58,360 --> 00:14:00,020
Yeah...so-so.

191
00:14:00,020 --> 00:14:01,860
Hey, Ryusuke.

192
00:14:01,860 --> 00:14:03,360
Huh? Takano-san.

193
00:14:03,360 --> 00:14:06,030
Oh, Taira! It's been awhile.

194
00:14:06,030 --> 00:14:09,030
Damn, your hair has grown.

195
00:14:09,030 --> 00:14:13,540
Ah, this? I know. I used to be bald.

196
00:14:13,540 --> 00:14:17,540
-How's Fire Joker?
-We disbanded last year.

197
00:14:17,540 --> 00:14:19,180
Disbanded?

198
00:14:19,180 --> 00:14:20,840
Yeah...

199
00:14:20,840 --> 00:14:24,580
I was 27 when we formed the band

200
00:14:24,580 --> 00:14:29,020
and I swore I wouldn't cut my
hair until we had a major debut.

201
00:14:30,720 --> 00:14:32,590
-Ah...
-Hmm...

202
00:14:34,890 --> 00:14:36,660
Where's Koyuki?

203
00:14:36,660 --> 00:14:38,500
Huh? Where'd he go?

204
00:14:38,500 --> 00:14:40,160
Weren't you together?

205
00:14:40,160 --> 00:14:42,500
Yeah...for a bit.

206
00:14:42,500 --> 00:14:45,840
Don't badmouth Kenji-san.

207
00:14:45,840 --> 00:14:46,670
Huh?

208
00:14:46,670 --> 00:14:51,180
He may not look it,
but he's tops in maintenance.

209
00:14:51,180 --> 00:14:52,140
'Kay.

210
00:15:02,850 --> 00:15:04,690
Hey, what's up?

211
00:15:04,690 --> 00:15:06,360
Like it?

212
00:15:06,360 --> 00:15:08,360
Try it out.

213
00:15:08,360 --> 00:15:10,190
I feel...

214
00:15:10,190 --> 00:15:14,360
I feel as though the guitar is calling me.

215
00:15:14,360 --> 00:15:15,870
A Telecaster?

216
00:15:15,870 --> 00:15:18,700
But you've got to wonder
what kind of condition it's in.

217
00:15:18,700 --> 00:15:20,200
You're right.

218
00:15:20,200 --> 00:15:21,370
Kenji-san...

219
00:15:21,370 --> 00:15:26,210
Well, if you buy it,
I'll replace the bridge and peg.

220
00:15:26,210 --> 00:15:29,050
Hmm...I'll even replace the pick-up.

221
00:15:29,050 --> 00:15:30,880
Really?

222
00:15:30,880 --> 00:15:32,880
But I...

223
00:15:32,880 --> 00:15:35,220
...don't have the cash.

224
00:15:35,220 --> 00:15:40,660
In the past, Taira came out to help
and really saved me a number of times.

225
00:15:40,660 --> 00:15:45,830
That's not the reason, but I'm
willing to make you a special loan.

226
00:15:45,830 --> 00:15:48,500
Thank you! I'll think about it.

227
00:15:48,500 --> 00:15:50,590
Hey Koyuki...Play it.

228
00:16:04,350 --> 00:16:08,850
G-Geez...I'm embarrassed
to play in front of you three.

229
00:16:08,850 --> 00:16:11,020
Why'd you act so shy?

230
00:16:11,020 --> 00:16:12,420
Well...

231
00:16:19,760 --> 00:16:23,720
"Chinese Restaurant Sing Lung"

232
00:16:24,200 --> 00:16:26,860
-Hurry it up.
-I'm sorry.

233
00:16:28,710 --> 00:16:31,540
Tanaka-kun...The dumplings?

234
00:16:31,540 --> 00:16:33,640
The customer is waiting.

235
00:16:35,380 --> 00:16:38,820
Hey, Tanaka, put your back into it.

236
00:16:38,820 --> 00:16:41,380
-Right!
-Hurry with the spring rolls!

237
00:16:48,160 --> 00:16:50,130
Two more hours.

238
00:17:06,840 --> 00:17:08,740
Ouchie!

239
00:17:18,860 --> 00:17:22,530
Hey part-timer! I'm making
the soup, so crack the eggs.

240
00:17:22,530 --> 00:17:23,990
Oh, right!

241
00:17:52,490 --> 00:17:56,390
In this world, even someone
so amazing couldn't turn pro...

242
00:17:58,330 --> 00:18:02,700
His hair was so long.

243
00:18:04,900 --> 00:18:07,870
"Sant 'Himizu"

244
00:18:24,690 --> 00:18:26,210
Ow...

245
00:18:34,870 --> 00:18:37,060
Huh? If it isn't Tanaka-kun!

246
00:18:37,970 --> 00:18:39,140
What're you doing?

247
00:18:39,140 --> 00:18:41,310
I deliver papers.

248
00:18:41,310 --> 00:18:43,970
By the way, are the tickets selling?

249
00:18:43,970 --> 00:18:46,640
No...I've been busy
with band rehearsals

250
00:18:46,640 --> 00:18:48,150
and haven't done a thing.

251
00:18:48,150 --> 00:18:50,480
Hey, that's bad!

252
00:18:50,480 --> 00:18:52,820
You have to help, too, Kikata-kun!

253
00:18:52,820 --> 00:18:56,190
Oh, I have to deliver
my newspapers. See you!

254
00:18:56,190 --> 00:18:56,950
Huh?

255
00:19:15,840 --> 00:19:17,470
Hey! What's going on?

256
00:19:18,680 --> 00:19:21,510
I told you, I was so busy,
I couldn't sell tickets.

257
00:19:21,510 --> 00:19:22,850
Oh...

258
00:19:22,850 --> 00:19:24,510
Come to the club office.

259
00:19:27,020 --> 00:19:30,610
I warned him! This is bad! This is bad!

260
00:19:34,520 --> 00:19:38,460
Is this club for light music?

261
00:19:38,460 --> 00:19:42,630
-Of course!
-We all have perfect music sense.

262
00:19:42,630 --> 00:19:44,300
Oh...

263
00:19:44,300 --> 00:19:47,500
No, these guys aren't like Hyodo.

